---
import SiteLayout from "@layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Jenna Meade – Good job."
  description="Design and development work by John Basham."
  home={false}
>
  <div class="archive-page">
    <article
      class="category-case-study format-standard has-post-thumbnail hentry post post-100 status-publish tag-brand tag-web type-post"
      id="post-100"
      itemprop="blogPost"
      itemscope
      itemtype="https://schema.org/BlogPosting"
      role="article"
    >
      <header class="article-header entry-header">
        <div class="post-tag">
          <span>Brand</span>
        </div>
        <div class="post-tag">
          <span>Web</span>
        </div>
        <div class="post-cat">
          <span>Case Study</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="entry-title single-title" itemprop="headline">
          Jenna Meade
        </h1>
      </header>
      <section class="entry-content" itemprop="articleBody">
        <div class="featured-image">
          <label for="expand-toggle" id="expand-image">
            <img
              alt="Screenshot of the homepage"
              class="attachment-full size-full wp-post-image"
              decoding="async"
              fetchpriority="high"
              height="1020"
              sizes="(max-width: 1650px) 100vw, 1650px"
              src="/uploads/2018/12/case-study-jenna-meade-1650.jpg"
              srcset="
                  /uploads/2018/12/case-study-jenna-meade-1650.jpg          1650w,
                  /uploads/2018/12/case-study-jenna-meade-1650-300x185.jpg   300w,
                  /uploads/2018/12/case-study-jenna-meade-1650-768x475.jpg   768w,
                  /uploads/2018/12/case-study-jenna-meade-1650-1024x633.jpg 1024w
                "
              width="1650"
            />
          </label>
        </div>
        <p>
          <small>
            <strong>Website:</strong>
            <a href="https://jennameade.com.au/">jennameade.com.au</a>
          </small>
          <br />
          <small>
            <strong>Services:</strong> design, develop, deploy, optimise,
            seo-setup
          </small>
        </p>
        <hr class="wp-block-separator" />
        <p>
          <strong>Design</strong>
        </p>
        <p>
          Jen has been well established as a journalist for years now, yet never
          had a home to collate all those years worth of writing.
          <a href="https://jennameade.com.au/writing/">Until now!</a>
        </p>
        <p>
          We sat down and went over everything, and I mean everything. Then we
          stood back and took a minimalist approach, basically stripping back
          everything to its most basic form and removing anything that was not
          absolute in its necessity.
        </p>
        <p>
          What we were left with was a simple flyer like home and contact page
          in one. It gets straight to the point telling you what she does and
          what she’s all about. Let’s you know she’s worked with some top notch
          publishers and gives you quick access to contact her.
        </p>
        <p>
          The rest of the site is aimed at providing a pleasurable reading
          experience for her writing; both on mobile and desktop. The small
          things add up here, character length of sentences, font choice, size
          and color contrast for legibility. They all go unnoticed by the
          untrained eye but affect the users experience on the website.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Develop &gt; Deploy &gt; Optimise</strong>
        </p>
        <p>
          This build began about a month before wordpress 5.0 was released, they
          always release a new theme alongside it. So to get an insight into
          what devs from wordpress themselves are doing I grabbed the as-yet
          unreleased
          <a href="https://codex.wordpress.org/Twenty_Nineteen">
            Twenty Nineteen
          </a>
           from
          <a href="https://github.com/WordPress/twentynineteen">github</a>. 
          Digging into its code it’s actually based off the
          <a href="https://underscores.me/">_s</a> theme which is several years
          old now. It goes to show good coding standards will stand the test of
          time.
        </p>
        <p>
          There were a few  minor issues being using a pre-release, namely
          javascript things. I basically stripped out what I didn’t need and got
          the site up to speed.
        </p>
        <figure class="alignnone size-full wp-block-image wp-image-108">
          <img
            alt="GTMetrix Score"
            class="wp-image-277"
            decoding="async"
            height="133"
            sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px"
            src="/uploads/2018/12/Screen-Shot-2018-12-18-at-1.21.05-pm-1024x133.png"
            srcset="
                /uploads/2018/12/Screen-Shot-2018-12-18-at-1.21.05-pm-1024x133.png 1024w,
                /uploads/2018/12/Screen-Shot-2018-12-18-at-1.21.05-pm-300x39.png    300w,
                /uploads/2018/12/Screen-Shot-2018-12-18-at-1.21.05-pm-768x100.png   768w,
                /uploads/2018/12/Screen-Shot-2018-12-18-at-1.21.05-pm.png          2028w
              "
            width="1024"
          />
          <figcaption>
            The homepage is running really smooth here with a good score.
            Further improvements to the theme and how it handles images could
            improve the score even more.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
